    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i just updated our A records for the main client site but it's still pointing to the old server on my end even though i cleared my local cache. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually show up everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "DNS changes can take time to propagate worldwide due to the global network of DNS servers and the potential for caching and propagation delays. When you update an A record, it may take up to 72 hours for the change to make its way globally. This is because many organizations, including internet service providers, ISPs, and web hosting companies, cache DNS records, slowing down the update process. Additionally, there may be regional or local holdouts, which further delay the propagation of the change.",
